ProductUnhunt — content license
==============================

Copyright (c) 2026 Ravi Kumar Singh and the individual contributors named in
each entry's frontmatter. All rights reserved.

This license covers everything under `src/content/` — the ideas, their prose,
their taglines, and their editorial stamps. The site's software is separately
MIT-licensed; see the `LICENSE` file at the repository root.

The repository is public so that ideas can be submitted as pull requests and
so that comments can be backed by its Discussions. Public is not the same as
unlicensed. Nothing here is placed in the public domain, and being able to
read or fork this repository on GitHub does not grant a license to republish
its contents elsewhere.

WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

  - Read it. Link to it. Send it to someone who deserves it.
  - Quote a reasonable excerpt — a tagline, a paragraph — with attribution to
    ProductUnhunt and a link to the idea it came from.
  - Fork this repository on GitHub to prepare a contribution back to it.

WHAT REQUIRES WRITTEN PERMISSION

  - Republishing an idea, in whole or in substantial part, anywhere else.
  - Deploying this content as a site of your own, under any name.
  - Any commercial use, including advertising-supported reposting, and
    including collections, compilations, or "best of" aggregations.
  - Training or fine-tuning a machine learning model on this content.

CONTRIBUTED IDEAS

Contributors keep the copyright in the ideas they submit. By submitting, a
contributor grants ProductUnhunt a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide licence
to publish, edit, translate, and roast the submission, and to keep it
published. See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

That grant runs to ProductUnhunt. It does not run to you, and forking this
repository does not put you in ProductUnhunt's position.

PERMISSION

Ask: ideas@productunhunt.com. The answer is usually yes, and always
unenthusiastic.
